<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26344" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">leucăcantha</span></b> , ae,
		f., and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">leucă-canthos</span></b> , i, m., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λευκάκανθα</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The white thorn</i>, form leucacantha, <i><span class="en">Plin. 22,
				16, 18, § 40</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">form leucacanthos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					21, 16, 56, § 94</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A plant</i>, called also phalangites and
			leucanthemon, <i><span class="en">Plin. 27, 12, 98, §
		124</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
